From: Vibe <vibe@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:01:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Revise patch transfer protocol: plain-text default +
 push-back repair loop; base64 as fallback

Two verified sender-side slip incidents in base64 payloads: eqLambertian.b64
(f65f439/39e3635) had an insertion (77-char dciIg line -> stream shift ->
base64 'invalid input') plus two silent substitutions; the CONTEXT.md patch
chunk_aa (receiver evidence in 416dcfb) had a single substitution corrupting
one quantum inside an ADDED diff line, so git am applied it silently and only
the per-chunk sha256 caught it. Plain patches fail loudly ('corrupt patch at
line N'), so they are now the default, gated by sha256 + git apply --check,
with a repair loop (receiver pushes the received file to transfer/failed/,
sender fetches, diffs locally, sends only a minimal correction).
